  "slug": "promote-topic-0ce2",
  "summary": "New work links distinct adaptors, tethers and condensates to organelle quality control under starvation, iron loss and lysosomal damage.",
  "synthesis": "Most items describe organelle remodeling under stress through autophagy or related quality-control routes, but the compartments, stresses and effectors differ. Contact-phagy uses SIGMAR1-CCPG1 to turn over ER-mitochondria contact-site subdomains. Iron deficiency drives pexophagy via GABARAP-FLCN/FNIP1 and TFEB/TFE3 activation. Yeast Mdm1 balances phospholipid and neutral lipid metabolism to allow autophagosome completion. Processing bodies and stress granules support lysosomal quality after damage, while RAB11-RAB30 uses phosphoinositide turnover for endosomal remodeling and survival. NRF2-dependent autophagy clears lipofuscin-like granules in RPE cells, and the axon initial segment gates lysosome trafficking via MCF2L. The GCase-deficiency study adds impaired macropinocytic uptake of α-synuclein ectosomes by astrocytes. What is new is the assignment of specific adaptors, tethers and condensates to each context, not a single shared mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
